        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    annual_dividend = 0.5\n    dividend_growth_rate = 0.06\n    required_rate_of_return = 0.10\n\n    # Calculate the terminal value at the end of year 2\n    year_3_dividend = annual_dividend * (1 + dividend_growth_rate)\n    terminal_value = year_3_dividend / (\n        required_rate_of_return - dividend_growth_rate\n    )\n\n    # Discount the dividends and terminal value to the present\n    equity_value = (\n        annual_dividend / (1 + required_rate_of_return)\n        + (annual_dividend + terminal_value)\n        / (1 + required_rate_of_return) ** 2\n    )\n\n    # return answer\n    return round(equity_value, 3)\n```",
